<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 137,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 137,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Wednesday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 17,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 20,000 tonnes of Australian barley in its weekly tender.</p>
<p>The Australian wheat was for November shipment while the remainder was for December shipment.</p>
<p>Details of the tender results are as follows (in tonnes):  Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000	   Western white	    40,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   20,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter	  20,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  25,000</p>
<p>				   Durum			15,000</p>
<p> Australia   17,000	  Prime hard		 17,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> Australia   20,000	   Feed			20,000</p>
</text>
